{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1608493,"ns":0,"title":"Experimenter's regress","extract":"In science, experimenter's regress refers to a loop of dependence between theory and evidence. In order to judge whether a new piece of evidence is correct we rely on theory-based predictions, and to judge the value of competing theories we rely on existing evidence.","description":"Loop of dependence between theory and evidence","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}